ONLINE OPTION
-------------

  The online option requests traveltime picks from the IRIS Traveltime Web
  Service.  All options are the same with the exception of a much broader
  array of traveltime that are able to be calculated

  First get some data from IRIS::

    SAC> data usgs:us1000gcii net IU cha BHZ sta WAKE dur 30m loc '00' read

  Get online traveltimes and set them in the header::

    SAC> SSS
    Signal Stacking Subprocess.
    SAC/SSS> traveltime online picks 0
    traveltime: depth: 600.000 km
    traveltime: setting phase P        at 404.5600 s [ t = 404.5600 s ] t0
    traveltime: setting phase PKiKP    at 942.3000 s [ t = 942.3000 s ] t1
    traveltime: setting phase PcP      at 513.8800 s [ t = 513.8800 s ] t2
    traveltime: setting phase S        at 729.0000 s [ t = 729.0000 s ] t3
    traveltime: setting phase SKiKS    at 1311.0500 s [ t = 1311.0500 s ] t4
    traveltime: setting phase ScS      at 942.3400 s [ t = 942.3400 s ] t5

  Get online traveltimes for the PREM model for specific phases::


    SAC> SSS
    Signal Stacking Subprocess.
    SAC/SSS> traveltime online picks 0 model prem phases P pP sP PcP PKiKP
    traveltime: depth: 600.000 km
    traveltime: setting phase P        at 404.2200 s [ t = 404.2200 s ] t0
    traveltime: setting phase PKiKP    at 940.2500 s [ t = 940.2500 s ] t1
    traveltime: setting phase PcP      at 513.1900 s [ t = 513.1900 s ] t2
    traveltime: setting phase pP       at 505.5100 s [ t = 505.5100 s ] t3
    traveltime: setting phase sP       at 574.1700 s [ t = 574.1700 s ] t4

  Get online traveltimes for the PREM model for only P and S. The CLEAR
  keyword truncates the list of phases from previous commands::


    SAC> SSS
    Signal Stacking Subprocess.
    SAC/SSS>  traveltime online picks 0 model prem phase clear P S
    traveltime: depth: 600.000 km
    traveltime: setting phase P        at 404.2200 s [ t = 404.2200 s ] t0
    traveltime: setting phase S        at 728.6300 s [ t = 728.6300 s ] t1

